            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0357" n="314" xml:id="pg314"/>

                <head>124. Backchannel Message From the
                    Ambassador to Chile (Korry) to the
                    President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs (Kissinger)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d124-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Santiago</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1970-09-27">September 27,
                        1970</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>1. Following two items spell the end of the ball game here in Chile. We now move
                    into a denied area condition:</p>
                <p>a. [<hi rendition="#italic">name not declassified</hi>] told me morning 27
                    September that Anaconda New York has refused to go along with his suggestions,
                    believing that Chile is lost and no further maneuvering warranted. He got call
                    at 0200 hours saying “ball game over. No use trying to quarterback now.”</p>
                <p>b. British Ambassador Hilyard told me same morning that he had recently
                    requested, and had just received authorization to offer, a total of four million
                    pounds sterling from a group of British private banks. Hilyard has told both
                    present government and Allende of this
                    credit.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
